comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T22:10:10.109Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict 3130-item all-status corpus and live warning/JSON stderr searches found completed related output-format and recurrence work but no exact active owner for this observed Windows failure. Intake only, open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-26T22:10:48.773Z","harness:codex",The current continuation independently read the complete hosted failure log and linked the source alert. A later local Linux full-suite run passes the existing handler-error test; that does not establish the native Windows warning producer or a fix. Reproduction and native hosted proof remain necessary. No implementation claim is taken.
  "2026-10-29T08:28:16.039Z","harness:codex","Nightly run 40837931196 at 2016f0e6870b4631bf2e0f4bfb0fbe983556c3ea reproduces the existing Windows shard 3/4 warning:se prefix before the extension handler JSON refusal; exit status remains 1. Investigating the actual producer and retaining full synthetic-fixture stderr in the next native run before attributing cause. Required PR checks otherwise passed except the separately corrected tracker expected-result gate."
  "2026-10-29T08:31:54.598Z","harness:codex","Added an assertion message containing complete synthetic-fixture stderr before JSON parsing. The test still requires exactly one JSON envelope, command_failed, exit1 and handler-boom; this is diagnostic evidence only, not a claimed fix. No warning producer has yet been established from the native log."
  "2026-10-29T09:02:56.608Z","harness:codex","A real CLI negative control now reproduces the framing failure deterministically on Linux: pass a synthetic Windows home file path to the same throwing extension handler. The native-path control passes; windows-home emits warning:secret_guard_detected:1:rules=absolute_home_path followed by the otherwise correct command_failed envelope and exit1. The public SDK evaluateMutationGuard independently returns that same advisory for the path. Implementing invocation-scoped deferred preflight warnings so JSON failures keep one envelope with warnings and handler detail, while successful invocations retain a structured warning diagnostic."
  "2026-10-29T09:16:24.646Z","harness:codex","The completed focused CLI cohort passes254 tests across four files, including the deterministic Windows-home refusal and a successful guarded mutation. Deferred warnings retain stable codes plus additional remediation text in warning_details, preserve existing diagnostics, and remain isolated across nested/concurrent invocations. Typecheck ESLint and docstring checks pass. The first local full run exposed two test expectation issues (nested create item ID and retaining settings remediation); both were corrected without weakening behavior."
  "2026-10-29T09:17:26.302Z","harness:codex","Native provenance is now confirmed: completed Windows Node24 shard3/4 job123349964084 in run40844923634 exposes warning:secret_guard_detected:1:rules=absolute_home_path before the JSON command_failed refusal on both attempts. This matches the deterministic Windows-home negative control exactly; no settings-read or Sentry cause is inferred. The guarded path is a synthetic fixture under the Windows runner home. The pending revised native run must prove the complete cohort with the transport fix."
  "2026-10-29T09:28:09.234Z","harness:codex",Current source943470bca is dispatched as Nightly40849657299. The previous watcher exited on GitHub REST quota exhaustion while Windows shard1 remained unfinished; it was not an all-jobs completion receipt. The new dispatch supersedes the old workflow under its existing concurrency rule. Completed Windows shard3 failure evidence remains retained; acceptance requires the full revised native cohort to finish successfully.
  "2026-10-29T09:38:20.808Z","harness:codex",Updated linked-test execution test-local-mvtcjlk5-ic30gx passes both commands after the transport fix. Graph-composition and record-integrity assurance pass; the bounded mutation gate retains345 killed and7 documented equivalent mutants with no unexplained survivors. Repository validation reports zero history drift across3151 items while retaining170 historical closure-metadata warnings; those historical records were not fabricated or mass-rewritten.
  "2026-10-29T10:35:41.322Z","harness:codex","Native Windows proof at 943470bca: Nightly run 40849657299, Windows Node 24 shard 3/4 job 123368461234 passed 3123 tests across 221 files, with 20 platform skips. The 78-test CLI integration file passed, including the previously failing extension-handler JSON framing scenario and its Windows-home control. All four Windows shards passed on this source. The whole superseded workflow was later canceled because other shards were canceled by the newer dispatch; this is a bounded native-job receipt, not a complete final-head workflow claim."
  "2026-10-29T11:11:42.620Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit review5696693853 identified npm-package-relative tracker links in the new configuration guidance. Both new references now use canonical public GitHub file URLs and explicitly state that tracker records are excluded from npm, preserving usable documentation in an installed package."
  "2026-10-29T13:33:02.052Z","harness:codex","The latest Windows shard3 run40864851705/job123416907459 again passes the78-test CLI integration cohort, including the real Windows-home advisory/error envelope. The whole shard fails solely because the unrelated compound receipt-settlement case exceeds30000ms on both attempts; this is not a full-shard pass and the original log is retained. CodeRabbit completed its full review of053da6b1c at12:11 UTC with no new findings."
  "2026-10-29T14:13:54.667Z","harness:codex","Review 5698771333 also identified missing TypeScript diagnostics fields. Added a shared preflight-warning shape to JsonErrorEnvelope and the attachment helper return type, plus compile-time consumer checks for stable string codes and structured remediation. This is an additive type correction; the wire representation and invocation behavior are unchanged."
  "2026-10-29T14:37:59.499Z","harness:codex",The direct TypeScript negative control against 3c5367550 fails with TS2339 for warnings and warning_details on JsonErrorEnvelope and the helper return type. Current typecheck passes with the additive optional diagnostics interface and preserves the original payload fields. The focused runtime cohort passes; no warning wire shape or exit code changed.
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T09:39:52.308Z","harness:codex","A truncated warning prefix is insufficient to attribute a native JSON failure. Preserve complete synthetic stderr first, reproduce the Windows home-path input independently, and retain the advisory with the command error instead of dropping it or weakening JSON parsing. Invocation-scoped buffering must preserve remediation text and isolate nested/concurrent CLI calls."
  "2026-10-29T10:46:57.439Z","harness:codex","Reproduce machine-readable transport failures with the actual warning producer and native path form. Keep advisory codes and remediation text inside an invocation-scoped collector, consume them into the existing failure envelope, and test nested/concurrent isolation, successful advisories, unchanged exit codes and human output. Truncated warning prefixes identify framing failure, not its cause."
